# r1113 Power Grid P2 boot 2 of 3 (same OUT as pwg2a.qb, restarted). Before boot (stopped):
#   python3 $INST/tools/scratch_query/qrun.py toml OUT/srv/pwg2/serverconfig/powergrid-server.toml electricity overheatedDropChance 0.0
pace 2

## SQ-PWG-20 | after the restart: same reads, wire counts, no load errors
> forceload add 990 990 1060 1090
sleep 6
> zpwgg read 1000 -60 1000
waitlog \[zpwgg\] done 30
> zpwgg read 1000 -60 1010 24
waitlog \[zpwgg\] read 30
> zpwgg wires 1000 -60 1000 8
waitlog \[zpwgg\] wires 30
sleep 1
expect \[zpwgg\] wires 5$
bootreject (Failed to|Exception).*(powergrid|TransmissionLine)
look compare with SQ-PWG-20a.log: same V, I (1 %), R and wire counts

## SQ-PWG-18b | chance 0: destroying the overheated gauge at Z 1040 drops nothing
> zpwgg overheated 1003 -60 1040 1
waitlog \[zpwgg\] overheated \d+ 30
expect \[zpwgg\] overheated at 1003 -60 1040
> setblock 1003 -60 1040 air destroy
sleep 3
> zpwgg items 1003 -60 1040 2
waitlog \[zpwgg\] items \d+ 30
expect \[zpwgg\] items 0

## SQ-PWG-15 | cut the 10 ohm loop: I=0, 4 wires
> zpwgg cut 1000 -60 1000
waitlog \[zpwgg\] done 30
sleep 2
> zpwgg read 1000 -60 1000
waitlog \[zpwgg\] read 30
sleep 1
expect \[zpwgg\] cut 1
expect \[zpwgg\] read .*wires=4
reject (Exception|/ERROR\])
look read I=0 (abs below 1e-6)

## SQ-PWG-13b | performance get after networks have solved (pwg2a's call came before any loop existed)
> powergrid performance get NetSolve
sleep 3
expect Last measurement
reject An unexpected error occurred

